WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.052
This is one of the most important slides in the
module ON

00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:10.333
and WHERE are not interchangeable in an outer join
The ON condition

00:00:10.359 --> 00:00:14.770
defines matching If we put a condition about lab
test name inside

00:00:14.796 --> 00:00:18.283
ON we are saying only glucose lab rows are eligible
to match

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:23.388
each patient Patients without glucose results can
still remain because the LEFT

00:00:23.414 --> 00:00:29.657
JOIN preserves them WHERE is evaluated on the joined
result If

00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:33.855
we filter where the right-side lab test name equals
Glucose unmatched patients

00:00:33.881 --> 00:00:38.486
have NULL on that right-side column NULL does not
satisfy the equality

00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:44.143
condition so those patients are removed That means a
LEFT JOIN followed

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:47.024
by the wrong WHERE condition can behave like an
INNER JOIN for

00:00:47.037 --> 00:00:52.196
that part of the logic A useful question is does
this condition

00:00:52.222 --> 00:00:55.788
describe which right-side rows may match or does it
describe which final

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.275
result rows I want to keep
